{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1207 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c010dc82619fcbc89552835bdae2ac9375578bfecd314a8954cbb6747be03e44" :edb/db-before-t 1206 :edb/db-after-t 1207 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534519 50 #inst "2026-10-12T01:44:39.255Z" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192327 1078 #edb/ref 17592186192328 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192617 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n$f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192617 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192617 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{0}^{3}x \\cdot \\frac{x^{2}}{9}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{3}\\frac{x^{3}}{9}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{36}\\right|_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192617 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192618 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4]$.\n\n$f(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 < x < 2$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192618 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 <        x <        2\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192618 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{S}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{2}x \\cdot \\frac{3x^{2}}{7}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{3x^{3}}{7}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{3x^{4}}{28}\\right|_{1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{45}{28}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[7X - 4] &= 7E[X] - 4 \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot \\frac{45}{28} - 4 \\\\\n&= \\frac{29}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192618 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{28}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[7X-4] & =7\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{45}{28}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192619 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X]$.\n${\\frac{1}{4},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < 2 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{4},\\end{vmatrix}2 \\le x \\le 3$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192619 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n![](images/98/98b997e3016e9ca5538863c3faa19ac017f90e8bcdeba40e09c03aba28c4ace4.svg)" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192619 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{0}^{3}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}x \\cdot f(x)dx + \\int_{2}^{3}x \\cdot f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}x \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}dx + \\int_{2}^{3}x \\cdot (\\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{3}{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}dx + \\int_{2}^{3}(\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - \\frac{3x}{4})dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{2}}{8}\\right|_{0}^{2} + \\left.(\\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{3x^{2}}{8})\\right|_{2}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{31}{24} \\\\\n&= \\frac{43}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186192619 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{31}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424086 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424088 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192676 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424089 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192677 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424085 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192677 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424087 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186192901 1050 780.0 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186193400 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186193400 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $E[3X - 4]$.\n\n$f(x) = \\frac{x}{8} - \\frac{1}{4}, 2 < x < 6$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186193400 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[3X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{4},\\,2<x<6\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186193400 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[3X-4]=3\\text{E}[X]-4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-4] & =3\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{14}{3}-4 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186193814 1064 "The **expected value** (also known as the **expectation** or **mean**) of a continuous random variable is the average value we'd expect to get if we observed the random variable many times.\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$, we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nFor example, consider the continuous random variable $X$ with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x}{4}, \\quad 1 < x < 3\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= \\int_{1}^{3}x \\cdot \\frac{x}{4}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{3}\\frac{x^{2}}{4}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{3}}{12}\\right|_{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{13}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 false] [17592186193814 1064 "The **expected value** (also known as the **expectation** or **mean**) of a continuous random variable is the average value we'd expect to get if we observed the random variable many times.\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, consider the continuous random variable $X$ with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x}{4}, \\quad 1 < x < 3\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{12}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424055 1080 "\\sqrt{e}" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424055 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424055 1083 #uuid "0e7252d1-7bec-51e8-895b-5c303264ccf4" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424056 1080 "-1" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424056 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424056 1083 #uuid "13c231a4-02c9-519e-a16e-fac887b7ebc8" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424057 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424057 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424057 1083 #uuid "26751660-b10c-52b5-b32b-8fb5a1bdd82c" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424058 1080 "\\frac{19}{9}" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424058 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424058 1083 #uuid "30c9587e-71e5-566c-a7c0-2ca7d8543d06" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424059 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424059 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424059 1083 #uuid "33e3d064-30ad-5eab-99b7-4055df83c43b" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424060 1080 "2" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424060 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424060 1083 #uuid "44d46d21-8790-5b62-b822-b15cfffb758c" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424061 1080 "15" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424061 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424061 1083 #uuid "493212b2