#edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424084 1077 "selection" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424084 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424074 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424084 1079 #uuid "c45ae753-611c-5337-a1ef-57b485b3183d" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424082 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1069 "q-130870" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}, & -\\sqrt{e}<x<-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & -1\\le x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1072 #uuid "0312f13e-9d46-503a-8af4-69a3bd5d2f16" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424085 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{|}_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}+{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}+\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424080 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1069 "q-90386" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1072 #uuid "3754a443-839d-5055-afd8-172b5271b8be" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424086 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{36}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424084 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1069 "q-130872" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1072 #uuid "713f9e9d-4bae-5fb8-b6da-37cc8d4aaf0e" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424087 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{6x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{5}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2x}{5}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2e}{5}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424081 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1069 "q-130751" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=6x(1-x),\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1072 #uuid "7821024d-c004-5d99-9790-91a65c2602fd" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424088 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot 6x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424083 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1069 "q-90455" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[8X-3].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9},\\,0<x<3\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1072 #uuid "a6256bcf-ce6c-599c-ab9b-d80ffcce67e9" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true] [17592186424089 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[8X-3]=8\\text{E}[X]-3\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[8X-3] & =8\\text{E}[X]-3 \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}-3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534519 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0e7252d1-7bec-51e8-895b-5c303264ccf4" 17592186424055 "answer-13c231a4-02c9-519e-a16e-fac887b7ebc8" 17592186424056 "answer-26751660-b10c-52b5-b32b-8fb5a1bdd82c" 17592186424057 "answer-30c9587e-71e5-566c-a7c0-2ca7d8543d06" 17592186424058 "answer-33e3d064-30ad-5eab-99b7-4055df83c43b" 17592186424059 "answer-44d46d21-8790-5b62-b822-b15cfffb758c" 17592186424060 "answer-493212b2-48a2-5243-a9c9-38c8ad4f746e" 17592186424061 "answer-58440bd6-5f91-58ba-8252-d7a100bf2bbc" 17592186424062 "answer-6ddc91ad-5eb5-580c-aec8-05f1a65ef396" 17592186424063 "answer-73b5e0f3-2a9f-5fb2-98c7-0b0e8e8b99a2" 17592186424064 "answer-77b11337-68cc-5792-80b0-2420a4a46582" 17592186424065 "answer-7ab28cb4-c411-518a-b8f9-3b843cb43bb2" 17592186424066 "answer-828c703f-f7c1-5221-a107-3b628a52c6ba" 17592186424067 "answer-90ca78b7-c93c-5e6a-8cc5-7647d2cc2740" 17592186424068 "answer-91379b67-0509-5582-a25b-36b84489